      "content": "I'm looking at a section of new asphalt pavement here in Phoenix that's showing premature longitudinal cracking. Given the high ambient temperatures we get, I'm trying to narrow down the primary drivers. Can you provide a summary of the key factors that contribute to longitudinal cracking in asphalt, specifically regarding thermal expansion, bitumen viscosity, and subgrade compaction?",
